Disable PROTECTED_MEMORY_ENABLED for mingw clang builds.

Chromium's base/BUILD.gn enables PROTECTED_MEMORY_ENABLED when
is_clang is true on Windows. The Windows code path in
base/memory/protected_memory.h relies on:

  #pragma comment(linker, "/SECTION:prot,R")

to mark the `prot` PE section read-only at link time. This pragma is
an MSVC linker directive; mingw ld ignores it. As a result the prot
section keeps its default read-write attributes, and
internal::CheckMemoryReadOnly later fails its

  CHECK((result > 0U) && (info.Protect == PAGE_READONLY));

assertion, abort()ing v8_context_snapshot_generator.exe with
STATUS_BREAKPOINT (0x80000003 / exit 2147483651) during

  blink::V8ContextSnapshotImpl::TakeSnapshot ->
  blink::RuntimeEnabledFeaturesBase::SetTestFeaturesEnabled ->
  base::ProtectedMemoryInitializer

The whole feature is a no-op on mingw GCC because is_clang is false
there, so the GCC build never hit this CHECK. Match that behaviour
for mingw clang by adding !is_mingw to the gate -- the read-only
guarantee is unreachable until either mingw ld learns the MSVC
pragma or chromium grows a portable alternative (e.g. an explicit
VirtualProtect on the section at startup).

--- a/src/3rdparty/chromium/base/BUILD.gn
+++ b/src/3rdparty/chromium/base/BUILD.gn
@@ -2670,7 +2670,13 @@ buildflag_header("protected_memory_buildflags") {
   header = "protected_memory_buildflags.h"
   header_dir = "base/memory"
 
-  protected_memory_enabled = !is_component_build && is_clang &&
+  # The Windows path relies on `#pragma comment(linker, "/SECTION:prot,R")`
+  # to make the prot section read-only at link time. mingw ld ignores that
+  # MSVC pragma, so the section stays writable and CheckMemoryReadOnly's
+  # CHECK fires at runtime (STATUS_BREAKPOINT in v8_context_snapshot_gen).
+  # Mingw GCC sidesteps this because is_clang is false; mingw clang has to
+  # opt out explicitly.
+  protected_memory_enabled = !is_component_build && is_clang && !is_mingw &&
                              (is_win || is_linux || is_android || is_mac)
 
   flags = [ "PROTECTED_MEMORY_ENABLED=$protected_memory_enabled" ]
